or $x ∈ R$, and let $f(x)$ be the $2π$-periodic extension of $F$ from $[MATH: x ∈ [- π, π)]$ to $x ∈ R$. The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$f(x)∼\\frac{a_{0}}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)(a_{n}\\cos (nx) + b_{n}\\sin (nx))$.\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient $a_{5}$ below, where $⟨, ⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[MATH: [- π, π).]$\n\n$(⟨\\sin (5x), \\sin (5x)⟩)/(⟨f(x), \\cos (5x)⟩)$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}}"}]}
